;;; `open` written as a fact's `:rule` clause loads, as a rule's name —
;;; regression `fact-clause`.
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ───────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `(p k :rule open)` says `p k` was derived by a rule named `open`.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; `open` is a name wherever the kernel does not read it, at the head of a
;;; written fact, a premise or a conclusion, and under an ordinary relation the
;;; head of a fact the kernel does not read (Q-M1f.66, Q-M1f.571): here it is
;;; written as a fact's `:rule` clause, so the program loads, and every command
;;; answers.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ───────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `f62e34e1`, release: the program loads, root holds `(p k)`, and R is 2
;;; states, exit 0 on every command.
;;; The engine loads it.
;;;

(relation a Thing :why "{?3} is an a")
(relation p Thing :why "{?3} is a p")
(relation q Thing :why "{?3} is a q")
(is-a k Thing)
(a k)
(p k :rule open)
